"""Gluing table: identifications of the same concept across branches.

Each concept lists its member nodes per branch by native id.  The roles
(layers) of the members are read from the data, not written here; where
they differ the concept is a *role flip* and the thesis lists it.

The table is curated by hand from the node labels and descriptions of the
released data files; every entry carries a one-line justification.  A node
belongs to at most one concept (checked by atlas.py).  Looser relations
(refinement, part-of, classical limit) are recorded separately as
CROSS_EDGES and are not identifications.
"""

